      "claim": "PNU-96391 absolute oral bioavailability was F = 0.6 (60%) in healthy volunteers, supporting F >= 20%.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "All high-transfer experimental evidence reports absolute oral bioavailability values above 20%, with no affirmative evidence for F < 20%. The query is a lipophilic, poorly soluble naphthoquinone, and the specified high-fat fed state is expected to enhance its absorption. The preponderance of transferable evidence therefore supports F >= 20%.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute bioavailability measurement for the query molecule is present in the supplied evidence.",
    "No analogue was tested specifically under a high-fat fed state, so the fed-state enhancement is inferred rather than directly evidenced.",
    "The analogue set is structurally diverse and does not include a close chemical relative of the query naphthoquinone."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
  "revision_action": "initial"
}

